# A GNU makefile is line-oriented text, not a Windows artifact: keep it LF in
# the working tree so analysers see the same bytes the index holds. The shell
# scripts are checked with shellcheck, which reads a carriage return as part of
# the command, and the Go toolchain is happier without CRLF either.
Makefile text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
